  "title": "# xLayout Opus phase (Big Dog orchestrator build `xlayout`, s4-s12) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice): go on…",
  "asked": "# xLayout Opus phase (Big Dog orchestrator build `xlayout`, s4-s12) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice): go on the Opus half of Molly. Brett approved the Fable -> Opus model switch: run `AXF_BUILD_PROFILE=big-dog node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs act approve xlayout <phase>` for the Build phase first. Based on branch claude/molly-fable (the Fable phase: shared dock engine + xlayout@1 asset type + unified chrome engine). Read its THREADS.md To carry on block for xLayout and `AXF_BUILD_PROFILE=big-dog node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs brief xlayout` for the full ask (Brett Nov 2 13:46 ET, in the build's detail). Fetch origin/main and merge it in first. Steps (tick each with act step xlayout <sN> done): s4 xLayout plugin scaffold in apps/molly: plugin.json, install/uninstall, Settings > Plugins > xLayout sub-tab (level toolbar), IDE mode switch s5 One banner + application menu + navigation menu + context menu covering the whole page in Molly; the user can't tell it's several apps s6 Guests (AmberX, axHub web, Console) send menus/nav/context/toolbars as data under Molly and hide their own; standalone each app stays exactly as now s7 IDE pane host on the dock engine: draggable, resizable, dockable panes; open-in-pane s8 Layout picker: the 10 preset pane layouts, preview before apply, pane limit enforced s9 Plugin toolbars: up to 3 per plugin/screen, show/hide, default location, in the plugin's settings s10 Toolbar designer as its OWN plugin (toolbar-designer): items from every plugin and screen, open target main/floating/pane; opened from the settings hook and right-click on any toolbar, through a capability service s11 Tests, check-theme/check-controls, help packs, lifecycle check s12 UI Review desktop + phone shots (--group \"xlayout - <Mon D h:mm AM/PM>\"), PR, THREADS Rules: one session, no sub-agents. Tokens only (--fx-*), framework controls, no var() fallbacks. Patches paused: don't touch it. Update the xLayout THREADS row each step. Commit + push branch claude/xlayout-opus often; open the PR at the end (push banner merges it). If claude/molly-fable's PR merges first, merge origin/main again before the PR. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
